  "data": {
    "body": "Let $L: \\mathbb{R}^{3} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation and $S=\\left\\{\\mathbf{v}_{1}, \\mathbf{v}_{2}, \\mathbf{v}_{3}\\right\\}$ be a basis for $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$, where\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}_{1}=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n1 \\\\\n1 \\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad \\mathbf{v}_{2}=\\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n1 \\\\\n0 \\\\\n-1\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad \\mathbf{v}_{3}=\\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n0 \\\\\n1 \\\\\n-1\n\\end{array}\\right] \\text {. }\n\\]\n\nSuppose that\n\n\\[\nL\\left(\\mathbf{v}_{1}\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n-2 \\\\\n1\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad L\\left(\\mathbf{v}_{2}\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n1 \\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad L\\left(\\mathbf{v}_{3}\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n1 \\\\\n-1\n\\end{array}\\right]\n\\]\n\nWhat is the standard matrix for the linear transformation $L$ (relative to the standard bases on $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$ and $\\left.\\mathbb{R}^{2}\\right)$ ?",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
